    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Motivated by Barro’s (2006) approach towards modeling the equity premium, we study the original formulation of the equity premium puzzle as posed by Mehra and Prescott (1985). Firstly, we build a single-regime stochastic model capable of simulating the effects of rare economic disasters. We then extend that into a multi-regime model which allows study of conditional disaster regimes and shocks that are not i.i.d., allowing for the simulation of a robust variety of economic phenomenon. Finally, we examine the results of modeling depression-recession economic cycles with the possibility of recessionary aftershocks following severe depressions. Compared to historical economic data, we conclude that a multi-regime model can account for the observed equity premium while simultaneously producing a plausibly low real rate.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
